            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-2332",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "org.eclipse.jetty/jetty-http: HTTP request smuggling via chunked extension quoted-string parsing"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In Eclipse Jetty, the HTTP/1.1 parser is vulnerable to request smuggling when chunk extensions are used, similar to the \"funky chunks\" techniques outlined here:\n  *  https://w4ke.info/2025/06/18/funky-chunks.html\n\n  *  https://w4ke.info/2025/10/29/funky-chunks-2.html\n\n\nJetty terminates chunk extension parsing at \\r\\n inside quoted strings instead of treating this as an error.\n\n\nPOST / HTTP/1.1\nHost: localhost\nTransfer-Encoding: chunked\n\n1;ext=\"val\nX\n0\n\nGET /smuggled HTTP/1.1\n...\n\n\n\n\n\nNote how the chunk extension does not close the double quotes, and it is able to inject a smuggled request."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-2332",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-2332\nSeverity: HIGH\nPackage: org.eclipse.jetty:jetty-http\nFixed Version: 12.1.7, 12.0.33\nLink: [CVE-2026-2332](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-2332)\nIn Eclipse Jetty, the HTTP/1.1 parser is vulnerable to request smuggling when chunk extensions are used, similar to the \"funky chunks\" techniques outlined here:\n  *  https://w4ke.info/2025/06/18/funky-chunks.html\n\n  *  https://w4ke.info/2025/10/29/funky-chunks-2.html\n\n\nJetty terminates chunk extension parsing at \\r\\n inside quoted strings instead of treating this as an error.\n\n\nPOST / HTTP/1.1\nHost: localhost\nTransfer-Encoding: chunked\n\n1;ext=\"val\nX\n0\n\nGET /smuggled HTTP/1.1\n...\n\n\n\n\n\nNote how the chunk extension does not close the double quotes, and it is able to inject a smuggled request.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-2332**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|HIGH|org.eclipse.jetty:jetty-http|12.1.7, 12.0.33|[CVE-2026-2332](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-2332)|\n\nIn Eclipse Jetty, the HTTP/1.1 parser is vulnerable to request smuggling when chunk extensions are used, similar to the \"funky chunks\" techniques outlined here:\n  *  https://w4ke.info/2025/06/18/funky-chunks.html\n\n  *  https://w4ke.info/2025/10/29/funky-chunks-2.html\n\n\nJetty terminates chunk extension parsing at \\r\\n inside quoted strings instead of treating this as an error.\n\n\nPOST / HTTP/1.1\nHost: localhost\nTransfer-Encoding: chunked\n\n1;ext=\"val\nX\n0\n\nGET /smuggled HTTP/1.1\n...\n\n\n\n\n\nNote how the chunk extension does not close the double quotes, and it is able to inject a smuggled request."
              },
              "properties": {
                "cvssv3_baseScore": 7.4,
                "cvssv3_vector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:H/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:N",
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "7.4",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "HIGH"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2024-6763",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "org.eclipse.jetty:jetty-http: jetty: Jetty URI parsing of invalid authority"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Eclipse Jetty is a lightweight, highly scalable, Java-based web server and Servlet engine . It includes a utility class, HttpURI, for URI/URL parsing.\n\nThe HttpURI class does insufficient validation on the authority segment of a URI.  However the behaviour of HttpURI\n differs from the common browsers in how it handles a URI that would be \nconsidered invalid if fully validated against the RRC.  Specifically HttpURI\n and the browser may differ on the value of the host extracted from an \ninvalid URI and thus a combination of Jetty and a vulnerable browser may\n be vulnerable to a open redirect attack or to a SSRF attack if the URI \nis used after passing validation checks."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-6763",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2024-6763\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: org.eclipse.jetty:jetty-http\nFixed Version: 12.0.12\nLink: [CVE-2024-6763](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-6763)\nEclipse Jetty is a lightweight, highly scalable, Java-based web server and Servlet engine . It includes a utility class, HttpURI, for URI/URL parsing.\n\nThe HttpURI class does insufficient validation on the authority segment of a URI.  However the behaviour of HttpURI\n differs from the common browsers in how it handles a URI that would be \nconsidered invalid if fully validated against the RRC.  Specifically HttpURI\n and the browser may differ on the value of the host extracted from an \ninvalid URI and thus a combination of Jetty and a vulnerable browser may\n be vulnerable to a open redirect attack or to a SSRF attack if the URI \nis used after passing validation checks.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2024-6763**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|org.eclipse.jetty:jetty-http|12.0.12|[CVE-2024-6763](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-6763)|\n\nEclipse Jetty is a lightweight, highly scalable, Java-based web server and Servlet engine . It includes a utility class, HttpURI, for URI/URL parsing.\n\nThe HttpURI class does insufficient validation on the authority segment of a URI.  However the behaviour of HttpURI\n differs from the common browsers in how it handles a URI that would be \nconsidered invalid if fully validated against the RRC.  Specifically HttpURI\n and the browser may differ on the value of the host extracted from an \ninvalid URI and thus a combination of Jetty and a vulnerable browser may\n be vulnerable to a open redirect attack or to a SSRF attack if the URI \nis used after passing validation checks."
              },
              "properties": {
                "cvssv3_baseScore": 3.7,
                "cvssv3_vector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:H/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:L/A:N",
                "cvssv40_baseScore": 6.3,
                "cvssv40_vector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:P/PR:N/UI:N/VC:N/VI:L/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N",
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "3.7",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "MEDIUM"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-11143",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "org.eclipse.jetty/jetty-http: org.eclipse.jetty: Security bypass due to differential URI parsing"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The Jetty URI parser has some key differences to other common parsers when evaluating invalid or unusual URIs. Differential parsing of URIs in systems using multiple components may result in security by-pass. For example a component that enforces a black list may interpret the URIs differently from one that generates a response. At the very least, differential parsing may divulge implementation details."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-11143",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2025-11143\nSeverity: LOW\nPackage: org.eclipse.jetty:jetty-http\nFixed Version: 12.0.31, 12.1.5\nLink: [CVE-2025-11143](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-11143)\nThe Jetty URI parser has some key differences to other common parsers when evaluating invalid or unusual URIs. Differential parsing of URIs in systems using multiple components may result in security by-pass. For example a component that enforces a black list may interpret the URIs differently from one that generates a response. At the very least, differential parsing may divulge implementation details.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2025-11143**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|LOW|org.eclipse.jetty:jetty-http|12.0.31, 12.1.5|[CVE-2025-11143](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-11143)|\n\nThe Jetty URI parser has some key differences to other common parsers when evaluating invalid or unusual URIs. Differential parsing of URIs in systems using multiple components may result in security by-pass. For example a component that enforces a black list may interpret the URIs differently from one that generates a response. At the very least, differential parsing may divulge implementation details."
              },
              "properties": {
                "cvssv3_baseScore": 3.7,
                "cvssv3_vector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:H/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:L/A:N",
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "3.7",
                "tags": [
